{"The `include_website_name` method is missing the trailing `?`, so ActiveModel::Serializer will not treat it as the inclusion hook for the `website_name` attribute, causing `website_name` to be serialized whenever it has a value regardless of inclusion conditions. Should be renamed to `include_website_name?`.": 0.22913338243961334, "`website_name` is derived directly from `website` but is not treated as an untrusted attribute, so low-trust users whose `website` is intentionally hidden via `untrusted_attributes` / `restrict_user_fields?` will still leak their website through `website_name`. A TL0 user viewed anonymously can have their website exposed via this new field.": 0.7372775077819824, "`website_name` should be subject to the same untrusted gating as `website` (by adding it to `untrusted_attributes` or checking `scope.restrict_user_fields?`).": 0.8580710291862488, "The new `website_name` specs only cover the happy path for a regular user and do not verify that `website_name` remains hidden for TL0 users viewed anonymously. Should add a spec in the existing 'with a TL0 user seen as anonymous' context that asserts `json` does not include a `:website_name` key when `untrusted_attributes` are filtered.": 0.7693487405776978}